      "title": "Nigerian security forces free more than 300 hostages in ‘largest single-day recovery’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/06/nigerian-security-forces-free-hostages-abducted-by-militants",
      "description": "<p>President hails operation to rescue captives held in dense forests of Kainji Lake national park in north-central region</p><p>Nigerian security forces have rescued more than 300 abducted people in what the president, Bola Ahmed Tinubu, hailed as the largest single-day hostage recovery in the country’s history.</p><p>The release was announced on Wednesday after a joint operation, conducted by the military, police and counter-terrorism units, freed victims held captive in the dense forests of the Kainji Lake national park in the north-central region.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/06/nigerian-security-forces-free-hostages-abducted-by-militants\">Continue reading...</a>",
